, 12.1.1, 12.1.2</span></span></span></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black;width:99px;padding:5px 5px 5px 5px;height:41px;background-color:white;border-top:none;border-right:2px solid black;border-left:none\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Replace log4j-2.13.3.jar with log4j-2.17.0.jar</span></span></span></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black;width:75px;padding:5px 5px 5px 5px;height:41px;background-color:white;border-top:none;border-right:2px solid black;border-left:none\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Upgrade to 12.1.3</span></span></span></td></tr></tbody></table><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'inherit' , serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Note: </span></span></span></strong>Vulnerability is considered as false positive for<strong> </strong>APLS version 10.7.0 to 11.6.0. Details available as part of question listed below - <em>Are APLS versions 10.7.0 to 11.6.0 are impacted with CVEs?</em></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Question:</span></strong><span style=\"color:black\"> Is AutoPass License Server (APLS) Impacted by CVE-2021-44228, CVE-2021-45046 and CVE-2021-45105?</span></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Answer:</span></strong><span style=\"color:black\"> Yes, Please refer the above table for Impacted APLS versions against CVEs</span><span style=\"color:black\">.</span></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Question: </strong>Is Patch Available for this?</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Answer</span></strong><span style=\"color:black\">: Yes, download the latest APLS version from Marketplace <span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"> <a href=\"https://marketplace.opentext.com/itom/content/autopass-license-server\">AutoPass License Server | ITOM Marketplace</a></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Question: </strong>For APLS version 11.7.0 to 12.1.0, is there Mitigation for this CVEs without Upgrade to latest version?</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Answer: </span></strong><span style=\"color:black\">Yes</span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Option1: </span></strong></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Replace the </span>log4j-*-2.13.3. jar with log4j-*-2.17.0.jar</span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Note: </strong>If you have already replaced log4j-*-2.13.3. jar with log4j-*-2.16.0. jar as mitigation for CVE-2021-44228 and CVE-2021-45046, Then replace log4j-*-2.16.0. jar with log4j-*-2.17.0. jar</span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Steps Below:</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">For Windows:</span></span><ol><li style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Stop the APLS service. Navigate to services and find for “AutoPass License Server” and stop. Refer below image for reference</span></span></span></li></ol><div style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><img src=\"/api/web/support/article/attachment/042c4248-f739-4fd2-9b28-4f3fb0394fa0\" width=\"984\" height=\"339\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" /></div><div style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">     2. Navigate to lib folder under APLS installation folder, (\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\)</span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">     3. Backup and remove three jar files log4j-core-2.13.3.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.13.3.jar, log4j-api-2.13.3.jar</span></span></span></span></div><img src=\"/api/web/support/article/attachment/81e31b14-6b3f-45b8-a657-36f53e765899\" width=\"624\" height=\"154\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" /><div style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">     4. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">Download and extract the</span><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman' , serif\"><u> </u></span></b></span><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><b style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman' , serif\">Log4j_2.17.zip</span></b></span> <span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">, you should find 3 jars in the extracted folder, </span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">log4j-core-2.17.0.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.17.0.jar, log4j-api-2.17.0.jar</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:8px\"> </div><div style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">     5. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">Copy these three jars</span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:black\">log4j-core-2.17.0.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.17.0.jar, log4j-api-2.17.0.jar to lib folder </span><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">(\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\)</span><br /><img src=\"/api/web/support/article/attachment/43eae451-1405-48fd-ae27-37816eff9e6a\" width=\"449\" height=\"162\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" /><br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">     6. start the service</span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:8px;margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">For Linux:</span></span></span><ol><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Stop the APLS service. Using below command</span></span></span></li></ol><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><em>service aplsLicenseServer stop</em></span></span></span><ol start=\"2\"><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Navigate to lib folder under APLS installation folder, (\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\)</span></span></span></li><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Backup and remove three jar files log4j-core-2.13.3.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.13.3.jar, log4j-api-2.13.3.jar</span></span></span></span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:11px;margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Download and extract the </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman' , serif\">Log4j_2.17.zip</span></span></strong></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">, you should find 3 jars in the extracted folder, <span style=\"color:black\">log4j-core-2.17.0.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.17.0.jar, log4j-api-2.17.0.jar</span></span></span></span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:11px;margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">Copy these three jars</span> <span style=\"color:black\">log4j-core-2.17.0.jar, log4j-slf4j-impl-2.17.0.jar, log4j-api-2.17.0.jar to lib folder </span>(\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\)</span></span></span></li><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Start the APLS service. Using below command</span></span></span></li></ol><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><em>service aplsLicenseServer start</em></span></span></span><div><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Question: </span></strong><span style=\"color:black\">Are APLS versions 10.7.0 to 11.6.0 are impacted with <strong>CVE-2021-45046, CVE-2021-44228 and CVE-2021-45105?</strong></span></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Answer</strong>: No, </span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">APLS version 10.7.0 to 11.6.0 uses log4j 1.2.15 for logging. In the (\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\) folder log4j-core-2.11 is present but it is not used by Application for logging. This is confirmed by certifying APLS version 10.7.0 to 11.6.0 by deleting log4j-core-2.11.jar<strong> </strong>file from the lib folder. Hence this is false positive for APLS version 10.7.0 to 11.6.0</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">This analysis is based on the bulletin below.</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">                 <a href=\"https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/security.html\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-family:'times new roman' , serif;color:#0563c1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><u><span style=\"font-family:'times new roman' , serif\">https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/security.html</span></u></a></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">               Extract from the bulletin:</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"> Note that only the log4j-core JAR file is impacted by this vulnerability. Applications using only the log4j-api JAR file without the log4j-core JAR file are not impacted by this vulnerability.</span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">                <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'helvetica' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Versions Affected: all versions from 2.0-beta9 through 2.12.1 and 2.13.0 through 2.15.0</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'helvetica' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">              Log4j 1.x mitigation</span></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'helvetica' , sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">: Log4j 1.x is not impacted by this vulnerability.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Recommendation for Customer using APLS version 10.7.0 to 11.6.0</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>OPTION 1: </strong></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Upgrade to latest version 12.1.3 which has fix for this vulnerability CVE-2021-44228 and CVE-2021-45046. We have upgraded to log4j-core-2.16.0</span></span></span><ol><li style=\"list-style-type:none\"><ol style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha\"><li style=\"margin-left:17px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">The version is backward compatible, this will support all the Micro Focus product which uses APLS 10.7.0 and above versions</span></span></span></li></ol></li></ol><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>OPTION 2:</strong></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Deleting the vulnerable log4j-core-2.11.0.jar from the \\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\ folder and restart the service will ensure that the APLS is not using vulnerable jars.</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Please note log4j-api-2.11 jar is not vulnerable and not deleted.</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Please find the below steps:</strong></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>For windows:-</strong></span></span><ol><li style=\"margin-bottom:11px;margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Stop the APLS service. Navigate to services and find for “AutoPass License Server” and stop. Refer below image for reference</span></span></span></li></ol><img src=\"/api/web/support/article/attachment/f142a3b8-e7ae-4b23-a409-d7cbe25657a2\" width=\"624\" height=\"213\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">    <strong>2.</strong>  Navigate to lib folder under APLS installation folder, (\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\) and DELETE log4j-core-2.11.0.jar ONLY.<br /><img src=\"/api/web/support/article/attachment/d677efee-1bf4-4904-9ab7-beaa78f65d05\" width=\"624\" height=\"109\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" /></span></span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">   <strong>3.</strong> Start APLS service from “Services” Window</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>For Linux:-</strong></span></span><ol><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Stop the APLS service. Using below command</span></span></span></li></ol><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><em>service aplsLicenseServer stop</em></span></span></span><ol start=\"2\"><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Navigate to lib folder under APLS installation folder, (\\autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps\\autopass\\WEB-INF\\lib\\) and DELETE log4j-core-2.11.0.jar ONLY</span></span></span></li><li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Start the APLS service. Using below command.</span></span></span></li></ol><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:105%\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><em>service aplsLicenseServer start</em></span></span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">Note: APLS 12.1.3 would be available to download from marketplace on 20 December 2021.</span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\"><strong>Question: </strong>log4j-core-2.x.jar version &lt;= 2.16 is present in autopass.war file and detected as vulnerability in security scans, what is the impact and how to mitigate this?</span></span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">The log4j-core.2.X.jar present in autopass.war file in webapps folder of autopass installation directory is not used by application, but it is part of web Archive (.WAR) of APLS installation and is used by Tomcat to unpack all the project files from the WAR file in a new directory named after the project (autopass). The files inside autopass.war is not used once it is unpacked, so log4j-core.2.x.jar present inside jar will not cause any issue and should be treated as false positive.<br /><br />If you must delete the war file to avoid scans reporting log4j.core-2.x&lt;=2.16, then please follow the below steps</span></span><br /><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'calibri' , sans-serif\">1) stop the Autopass License server service<br />2) Take the backup of autopass.war folder under “autopass\\apls\\apls\\webapps”<br />3) delete the .war file<br />4) Start the Autopass License server service<br />5) Verify that autopass folder is still present in webapps after restart<br />6) Access the application UI to confirm that autopass is started after restart</span></span><br /><br />To Delete the log4j.core-2.x&lt;=2.16 file from WAR file without deleting WAR file,<p>1) Stop the APLS service</p><p>2) In Windows: </p><p> open WAR file with WINRAR iand delete the WEB_INF\\lib\\log4j-core-2.x.jar and save it</p><p>In Linux use  command“zip -q -d autopass.war WEB-INF/lib/log4j-core-2.11.0.jar ” from webappas folder<br />Note: For APLS version 10.7 to 11.6.0 delete log4j-core-2.11.0.jar, from APLS version 11.6 to 12.1.0 delete log4j-core.13.3.jar</p><p>3) start the service<br /><br /></p></div></div></div></div></div></div>","ArticleType":"Security Bulletins","LastContentUpdateTime":1791995338077,"Version":22,"Votes":0,"Views":0,"RelatedArticles":[],"Attachments":[{"id":"log4j_2.17.0.zip","name":"log4j_2.17.0.zip","contentType":"zip","extension":"","size":1891796,"isExternalAttachment":true,"fileUrl":null,"url":"/api/web/support/article/s3-attachment/log4j_2.17.0.zip?articleId=1770456"}],"NumberOfAttachments":1,"Products":[{"Id":"1617157","DisplayLabel":"Service Virtualization","versions":[{"version":"5.1"},{"version":"4.2"},{"version":"2022 R1"},{"version":"3.1"},{"version":"3"},{"version":"25.3"},{"version":"2022 R2"},{"version":"2.1"},{"version":"4.1"},{"version":"5.3"},{"version":"All"},{"version":"26.1"},{"version":"3.7"},{"version":"3.8"},{"version":"5"},{"version":"2.2"},{"version":"2.3"},{"version":"2023"},{"version":"2"},{"version":"2022"},{"version":"3.5"},{"version":"2023 R1"},{"version":"5.4"},{"version":"3.6"},{"version":"4"},{"version":"5.2"},{"version":"Any"},{"version":"1"},{"version":"26.3"},{"version":"26.3"}]},{"Id":"1617672","DisplayLabel":"AutoPass License Server","versions":[]},{"Id":"1617775","DisplayLabel":"Application Lifecycle Management (ALM)","versions":[{"version":"TDV8.0"},{"version":"V9.x"},{"version":"24.1"},{"version":"16.0.1"},{"version":"17.0.1"},{"version":"26.1"},{"version":"16"},{"version":"17"},{"version":"15.5"},{"version":"25.1"},{"version":"15"},{"version":"12.6"},{"version":"V10.0"},{"version":"12.2"},{"version":"11.5"},{"version":"12.55"},{"version":"11"},{"version":"12"},{"version":"V9.0"},{"version":"All"},{"version":"12.5"},{"version":"TDV7.6"},{"version":"V8.x"},{"version":"Any"},{"version":"24.2"},{"version":"23.3"},{"version":"23.4"},{"version":"25.3"},{"version":"26.2"},{"version":"1"},{"version":"14"},{"version":"25.4"},{"version":"24.4"},{"version":"25.2"},{"version":"24.3"},{"version":"26.3"},{"version":"26.3"},{"version":"26.4"}]},{"Id":"1617924","DisplayLabel":"Operations Orchestration (OO)","versions":[{"version":"10.7"},{"version":"10.6"},{"version":"25.4"},{"version":"10.2"},{"version":"10.5"},{"version":"2020.08"},{"version":"25.2"},{"version":"10.1"},{"version":"9"},{"version":"10"},{"version":"2021.02"},{"version":"2023.05"},{"version":"2022.05"},{"version":"2019.07"},{"version":"2018.09"},{"version":"2018.05"},{"version":"10.70 and"},{"version":"2018.12"},{"version":"24.4"},{"version":"24.1"},{"version":"2019.11"},{"version":"9.2.x"},{"version":"2022.11"},{"version":"Any"},{"version":"2020.02"},{"version":"10.8"},{"version":"9.1.x"},{"version":"2"},{"version":"1"},{"version":"26.2"},{"version":"2021"},{"version":"25.3"},{"version":"10.22"},{"version":"23.4"},{"version":"2023.01"},{"version":"26.4"}]},{"Id":"1617986","DisplayLabel":"UFT One","versions":[{"version":"23.4"},{"version":"25.2"},{"version":"24.2"},{"version":"2022"},{"version":"Any"},{"version":"2021"},{"version":"15"},{"version":"2023"},{"version":"24.4"},{"version":"26.1"},{"version":"14.5"},{"version":"2021 R1"},{"version":"11"},{"version":"12"},{"version":"12.51"},{"version":"11.5"},{"version":"V10.0"},{"version":"12.5"},{"version":"All"},{"version":"14"},{"version":"13"},{"version":"1"},{"version":"26.3"},{"version":"26.3"}]}],"CreatedTime":1639444344000,"Entitlement":"","CanRead":"Public_c","PhaseId":"External"}}